# The rows of src/runtime/recipes/vulpen/library/parts/sound-record/SoundRecord.cpp, a call each (src/tools/bench/bench.py).

## SoundRecord.cpp/SoundRecord::bind
seconds -1 -> throws runtime_error: "seconds = -1: above 0, and at most 11184, as a WAV file holds no more"; asked ["param seconds read as float"]
seconds 0 -> throws runtime_error: "seconds = 0: above 0, and at most 11184, as a WAV file holds no more"; asked ["param seconds read as float"]
seconds 0.0001 -> ["param seconds read as float"]
seconds 1 -> ["param seconds read as float"]
seconds 11184 -> ["param seconds read as float"]
seconds 11185 -> throws runtime_error: "seconds = 11185: above 0, and at most 11184, as a WAV file holds no more"; asked ["param seconds read as float"]
seconds inf -> throws runtime_error: "seconds = 0: above 0, and at most 11184, as a WAV file holds no more"; asked ["param seconds read as float, refused"]
seconds nan -> throws runtime_error: "seconds = 0: above 0, and at most 11184, as a WAV file holds no more"; asked ["param seconds read as float, refused"]

## SoundRecord.cpp/SoundRecord::cook
a frame after it saved -> logged []
a.wav -> [0.1, -0.1, 0.2, -0.2, 0.3, -0.3, 0.4, -0.4, 0.5, -0.5]
b.wav -> [0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25]
bound again, a.wav still named -> logged []
bound with b.wav, its first frame -> logged []
five frames played -> logged ["info: saved <here>/b.wav"]
no file -> logged []
the frame a.wav was named -> logged []
three frames played -> logged []
three more, two of them wanted -> logged ["info: saved <here>/a.wav"]
